{
  "answer": "You can customize the response status code of a FastAPI endpoint by using the `status_code` parameter in the path operation function. This parameter accepts either an integer representing the HTTP status code or an `IntEnum` from Python's `http.HTTPStatus` for convenience. Here is an example:\n\n```python\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI, status\n\napp = FastAPI()\n\n@app.get(\"/items/\", status_code=status.HTTP_201_CREATED)\nasync def create_item():\n    return {\"message\": \"Item created successfully\"}\n```\n\nThis example uses `status.HTTP_201_CREATED`, which corresponds to the HTTP status code 201 (Created).",
